          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A basket model generally crisps more aggressively because the air is concentrated in a small chamber. Oven-style units trade some of that intensity for racks, capacity and the ability to bake and toast. If crispness is your top priority, buy a basket; if flexibility matters more, an oven-style unit is the better fit."
          }
