          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do air fryers use a lot of electricity?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not much for typical use. A 1,700-watt unit draws 1.7 kilowatts while heating, so a 20-minute cook is roughly half a kilowatt-hour, which costs pennies at average rates. For small batches it uses less energy than heating a full-size oven, and your own electricity rate determines the exact cost."
