        <div id="how-they-work" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What an Air Fryer Actually Does (It Isn't Frying)
          </h2>

          <p>
            An air fryer is a small convection oven with a very strong fan. A heating element sits above the food, and the fan drives hot air down and around it at high speed, so surface moisture leaves quickly and the outside browns. There is no oil bath involved, which is why the name oversells it. What you get is roasting, accelerated, inside a chamber small enough to preheat in a couple of minutes.
          </p>

          <p>
            That explains both what air fryers do well and where they struggle. Frozen fries, wings, breaded cutlets, roasted vegetables and reheated pizza all have dry, exposed surfaces that respond to fast airflow. Wet batter does not, because it drips off before it sets, and anything light enough to blow around, like a loose handful of herbs, can end up pressed against the element.
          </p>

          <p>
            The size and shape of the chamber matter more than the marketing. A basket model concentrates heat and airflow in a tight space, which usually means faster cooking and crisper edges but a smaller usable area. An oven-style unit spreads the same idea across racks, giving you capacity and versatility at the cost of gentler, slower airflow. Neither is better in the abstract; they suit different kitchens and different habits.
          </p>

          <p>
            Two other points shape any honest purchase. First, an air fryer rarely replaces a full-size oven. It replaces the oven for small jobs, which is a genuine saving in time and kitchen heat, but a roast for eight still wants the big cavity. Second, because the element sits close to the food, how thick the food is and how crowded the basket is will decide results far more than the number on the display.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
