        <div id="types" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. Basket vs Oven-Style vs Dual-Zone: Which Shape Fits Your Kitchen
          </h2>

          <p>
            The classic basket air fryer is a single drawer with a perforated basket inside. It is compact, preheats fast, stores easily and delivers the strongest airflow per square inch of food. The downside is that it cooks one thing at a time. A main and a side means either two rounds or stacking different foods together, and neither is ideal when dinner has to be ready at once.
          </p>

          <p>
            A dual-zone model solves that by putting two independent baskets in one body, each with its own temperature and timer. Many include a function that staggers the start times so both finish together, which is the feature that makes them feel like a different category. The price is footprint and cleanup: they are wide, and you are washing two baskets and two crisper plates every time you use both.
          </p>

          <p>
            Oven-style units, sometimes sold as air fryer toaster ovens, look like a toaster oven with a fan and an air-fry setting. Racks and trays give you real capacity, and most also toast, bake and broil, so they can replace a toaster oven rather than sit next to one. They are bulkier, preheat more slowly, and the crisping is a little less aggressive than a drawer fryer. Check the interior dimensions against the pans you own.
          </p>

          <p>
            The decision rule is simple. If you cook for one to three people and counter space is tight, buy a basket model. If you cook for four or more and want mains and sides together, buy a dual-zone model. If you want to retire a toaster oven and can spare roughly a foot and a half of counter, buy an oven-style unit. Do not choose oven-style just because it does more; if you mostly make fries and wings, a basket does them better.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
